[38;2;124;124;124mWhen $p_{\max} - 2$ IS prime (twin prime), the bottleneck moves to the second [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mlargest prime in $(n/2, n]$ that is not a twin prime.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor example:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $n=13$: $p_{\max}=13$, $13-2=11$ prime, so 13 is OK. Bottleneck is 11, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$11-2=9$ not prime.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $n=19$: $p_{\max}=19$, $19-2=17$ prime, so 19 is OK. Bottleneck is 17, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$17-2=15$ not prime.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $n=31$: $p_{\max}=31$, $31-2=29$ prime. Bottleneck is 29, $29-2=27$ not prime.[0m[38;2;124;124;124m- $n=43$: $p_{\max}=43$, $43-2=41$ prime. Bottleneck is 41, $41-2=39$ not prime.[0m[38;2;124;124;124m- $n=61$: $p_{\max}=61$, $61-2=59$ prime. Bottleneck is 59, $59-2=57$ not prime.[0m[38;2;124;124;124m- $n=73$: $p_{\max}=73$, $73-2=71$ prime. Bottleneck is 71, $71-2=69$ not prime.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mSo even when the largest prime is a twin prime, the second largest prime in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$(n/2, n]$ that is not a twin prime becomes the bottleneck.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key insight: for $n \ge 11$, there is always a prime $\ell \in (n/2, n]$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msuch that $\ell - 2$ is not prime, AND $\ell$ cannot be represented as $p + q$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mor $2\ell = p + q$ or $3\ell = p + q$ for primes $p < q \le n$.[0m

