[38;2;124;124;124m- (If $\ell \le 2n/3$) No two primes in $(n/2, n]$ sum to $3\ell$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about why this always happens. The largest prime $p_{\max} \le n$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mis in $(n/2, n]$ (Bertrand). If $p_{\max} - 2$ is not prime and $p_{\max} > [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2n/3$, done. If $p_{\max} - 2$ is prime, we need to look deeper.[0m

