[38;2;124;124;124m4. $n \ge 11$: fails because there's a prime $\ell \in (n/2, n]$ with [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$v_\ell(P(n)) = 0$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor part 4, I need to prove that for all $n \ge 11$, there exists a prime $\ell [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\in (n/2, n]$ such that $\ell \nmid (p+q)$ for all prime pairs $p < q \le n$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about how to prove this. The key insight is:[0m

